      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:208:5",
      "text": [
        " رَجُلٍ أَحْرَمَ فِي شَهْرٍ وَ أَحَلَّ فِي آخَرَ فَقَالَ يُكْتَبُ لَهُ فِي الَّذِي قَدْ نَوَى أَوْ يُكْتَبُ لَهُ فِي أَفْضَلِهِمَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hafs Bin Al Bakhtary, from Abdul Rahman Bin Al Hajjaj, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding a man who wears <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> during a month, and frees during another. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It would be Written for him regarding that which he intended, or would be Written for him regarding the superior of the two’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Flafs ibn al-Bakhtariy from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Hajjaj who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that a man who assumes the state of Ihram during a month and comes out of it during the next month, the Imam said, ‘This is counted al-‘Umrah in the month in which he has made his intention or al-‘Umrah in the more virtuous month.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
